; 07-instantiate-a-universal-fact.kurt
;
; Instantiate a universal fact
;
; Load `logic` for quantifier inference rules. A universally quantified fact can be instantiated
; at a particular value:

load logic
bool P
arity P 1                ; P takes one argument (declarations: lesson 20)
const P, c

use forall $x P($x)
P(c)

; `$x` is the bound variable. Instantiating it is built into Kurt, so `P(c)` follows directly from
; the fact and the output shows just `by 13`.
